    "proof": "The upper bound R_X<=pi(2X)^2 is O(X^2/log^2 X). For a lower bound on S_X, restrict the first prime p and odd composite semiprime m to (X/2,X]; then p+m lies in (X,2X]. PNT gives about X/(2 log X) such primes, while Landau's theorem gives about X log log X/(2 log X) such odd semiprimes; even semiprimes are lower order. Hence S_X is Omega(X^2 log log X/log^2 X). The exact identity C_X-L_X=2R_X proves the limit. A pointwise fixed delta would survive summation on every sufficiently large dyadic block, contradicting that limit.",
